WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.080
What makes your favorite League of Legends champion your favorite?

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.860
Is it their kit, their viability in the meta, or did you fall in love with

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.240
their personality and their character?

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:18.300
Well voice lines play a huge part in how that character comes across to us on the Rift.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.500
That's why I love playing Annie so much.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.780
Have you seen my bear Tibbers?

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.800
You smell like, burning.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.680
Beaten by a little girl.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:36.720
That's why this week we’re counting down the top 10 league of legends champions based on their voice lines.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:41.040
Now we’re gonna be fair with this one guys, one legendary one-liner

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.000
is not gonna land you at the top of our list.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.700
We're taking into account a champion's entire repertoire,

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.820
of lines.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.680
Now let's hear what the champions themselves have to say.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:58.140
Kicking off our list at number 10 is the Glorious Executioner himself.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.040
"Welcome to the League of Draven."

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.240
This egotistic narcissist has some of the most iconic voice lines in the game,

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.340
"Perfection? I got that."

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.000
"Draven's giving a master class in how to play Draven."

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.400
(Laugh)

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.940
which naturally, are all about himself.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.340
"It looks like Draven's taking a Draven break."

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.080
"Not Draven, Draven."

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.740
And why wouldn’t they be?

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.900
"Let's check out our OP players of the game."

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:32.180
"Draven, Draven, Draven, Draven and Draven."

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.340
He may have teammates… but who cares about them?

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.000
Especially with this axe juggling death machine tearing up the lane .

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.760
"Draven throwing the other team a bone."

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.360
"Who wants some Draven."

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:54.080
"Let's check out our featured matchup of the day, Draven vs. some loser."

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.700
"Sjokz better interview me after this."

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:01.200
His flair for the dramatic makes his voice lines some of the most famous in League of

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.160
Legends.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.740
"Draven was an excellent pick this game."

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:06.840
"And every game."

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.840
Earning this grim Noxian performer a spot on our list.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.980
"Did you know Draven can catch another Draven's axes?"

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.720
"You should read the hits more often."

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.740
Quirky doesn’t even begin to describe the ninth entry on our list.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.760
"A solid giggle should do the trick."

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:27.960
"Let's use all the colors."

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:31.980
Lulu takes the whimsy of the Yordles to a whole new level.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.240
"Cuddly incoming."

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.800
"Never look a tulip in the eye."

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.360
Her cutesy, fanciful voice lines certainly break the tension, even in the most

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.060
dramatic of teamfights.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.860
"I recommend skipping."

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:48.920
No matter how dangerous the situation, with a wave of her wand and some dubious magic

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:52.160
words the situation becomes, well, more cuddly.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.940
"Adoribus."

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.980
"Delightify."

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.340
"Transmogulate!"

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:03.880
With Pix by her side, there’s nothing the Fae Sorceress can’t twirl through.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.800
"I could go for a twirl... Whoa, whoa whoa ah, wooh!"

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.680
"Whoa dizzy."

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:16.040
Taking our number 8 spot is Kled, who, if we’re being honest is the embodiment of

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.160
your solo queue teammates.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.560
"I find courage unpredictable, it's total insanity you can rely on!"

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:25.700
"I don't need a team to start a teamfight."

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.380
"Holy sh*t where are we?"

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:33.840
This Yordle and his semi-trusty mount Skaarl know exactly when to fight, that is all

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:34.520
the time.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.940
"I'll kill em all!"

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.680
"Charge!"

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:43.940
Decorated, fearless and a little insane, Kled charges into every battle with only one goal

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:46.720
in mind — to rack up the kills.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.600
"I might have to jump off this lizard and put my boot in your watoosie!"

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.900
"Sure, I'll kill all of em myself!"

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.640
"Shh. It's time to get violent."

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.180
"Weird."

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:03.420
But at the end of the day, it seems that all Kled wants to do is “reclaim” his land — or

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.580
more accurately, conquer the world.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.240
"This land was made for me, and me alone."

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.700
"I'm from all over. It's next to nowhere and shut the hell up!"

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:14.760
Whether it’s his constant yelling ,

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.660
"My brain is full of weasels."

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.160
"The badgers demand your death."

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.880
or his love of tacos,

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:26.620
"After we finish murdering these folks, what do you think? Tacos? Yeah, tacos."

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.920
no one would argue with this Cantankerous Cavalier taking a spot on our list.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:36.360
"I don't have trouble communicating, words is just treacherous bastards."

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:43.000
Our number seven champion may say his own name even more than even Draven.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:48.760
"Mundo say his own name a lot, or else he forget! Has happened before."

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.280
"Mundo!"

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.840
This purple mad man has a flair for the completely insane

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.240
(laughs and slurps)

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:59.360
The monosyllabic monstrosity indiscriminately

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:02.720
smashes anything in his way no matter what lane you’re in.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.840
"Mundo smash!"

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.800
"Mundo will go where he pleases!"

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.360
And still somehow manages

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.580
to find time to run an international corporation?

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:18.620
"Mundo runs international corporation as he pleases."

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:23.780
This deranged, demonized, denizen of Zaun has immortalized his voice in the world of

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.040
League of Legends.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.520
"Mundo go this way!"

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.240
Why talk when you can just punch people?

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:35.720
Well, I guess if you’re Vi you can do both.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:39.060
"Punch first, ask questions while punching.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:44.760
Coming in at number 6 we have Piltover’s Finest — an ex-gang leader turned law enforcer.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:49.060
Alongside partner Caitlyn, Vi nails the bad cop persona.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.200
"Care for a spot of tea?"

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.260
"Or maybe a spot of punch in the face."

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:58.980
"We can either do this the hard way or... Oh wait no there's just the hard way."

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:04.580
Impulsive, short-tempered, and equipped with a pair of hextech gauntlets, this is a woman

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:06.600
you do not want to mess with.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:13.240
"Why can't I get a straight answer, it's always just, 'Oh no stop hitting me! Ow my face.'"

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.340
"I let my hands do the talking."

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:19.600
She’s busting her way out of the jungle, dashing through your frontline and sending

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.440
you straight into the air.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.320
"Yeah teamwork!"

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:26.640
"Vi, hah, stands for violence!"

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:31.640
This hextech powered peacekeeping punching-machine has smashed her way on to our list.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:35.360
"Here I come to save the day... or wreck it."

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.240
"One girl wrecking crew."

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:41.480
The wispy, whimsical, and slightly boy crazy

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:45.260
"I'm not boy crazy, I just don't have a boyfriend yet."

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:48.120
cosmic herald of Targon, Zoe comes in at number

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:49.320
5 on our list.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:52.240
"Something good is going to happen, with sparkles!"

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.880
"Nobody has to grow up if they don't want to!"

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.620
"Or maybe they do."

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:57.800
"I don't though."

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:03.220
After millennia playing within realities beyond human comprehension, The Aspect of Twilight

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:06.760
isn’t above having fun with her “Space Doggie.”

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:10.000
"Aww, I can hear my favorite wittle space doggy."

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.480
"Bad, bad space dragon! Bad!"

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:15.440
Or a good old fashion love triangle.

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:22.720
"Hi Ezreal! I mean- That is you over there, right? I'm over here. I'm Zoe... Never mind."

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:28.000
"I do not like yellow hair. And Demacia. And light magic. And everything about her!"

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:32.200
"But now how is he gonna be my first kiss? He's dead!"

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:37.260
But you’ll definitely think twice about taking her lightly if she catches you in a

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.200
Sleepy Trouble Bubble.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:50.420
(Stream)

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:53.960
Zoe’s playful interactions with the rest of the cast have helped her

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.920
skip into the top 5 on our list.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:00.420
"Heyyyy! I'm gonna have new friends, new friends here,

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.100
and it's gonna be awesome 'cause they are awesome

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:06.020
and we'll have an awesome party with cake and stuff!"

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:09.960
"Should I make chocolate mooncake or strawberry mooncake?

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.980
CHOCOLATE STRAWBERRY CAKE!!"

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:18.700
The Yordles that have made our list thus far may have all been a little crazy, but this

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:20.280
one takes the cake.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.720
"Captain Teemo on duty."

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.760
For our number 4 spot we’re featuring the beloved Swift Scout, Teemo.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.960
"Size doesn't mean everything."

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.960
"Never underestimate the power of the Scout's code."

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:38.500
Though small in stature with a cheerful personality, Teemo reminds us that looks can be deceiving.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:41.800
"Turns out, I got a proficiency in killing."

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.440
"Killing's all I'm good at."

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:49.720
And with his time on the Omega Squad, it becomes quite obvious that this little guy is a stone

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:51.680
cold, natural-born killer.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:55.400
"War didn't change me, I changed war!"

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.700
"Never. Get. Attached."

00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:59.920
"Let the poison do its work."

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.780
"Sight. Shoot. Reload."

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:09.280
From his blinding blow darts to noxious mushroom traps, Teemo uses poison in various disturbing

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:11.480
ways, keeping you on your toes.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:13.600
"Let 'em die slow."

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:17.880
Once sworn to the Bandle Scout’s Code, Teemo does not mess around when it comes to his

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:18.840
convictions.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:21.620
"Some masks you never take off."

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:25.000
But war, war changes everyone.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.540
"Nobody's innocent any more."

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:33.800
One of the first champions designed by Riot, Annie is a League of Legends staple

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.860
"You wanna play too? It'll be fun!"

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:39.420
And comes at number three on this list.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:44.240
"Ashes, ashes, they all fall down."

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:49.120
While still a child, Annie is not afraid to dish it out with the most powerful mages

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:50.800
"Play time!"

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:54.400
"Eeny, meeny, miny, burn!"

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.660
"Don't be a scaredy cat!"

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.780
Alongside her teddy bear Tibbers

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.800
"Have you seen my bear Tibbers?"

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:07.680
who is equal parts cuddly and terrifying, Annie incinerates the competition with a quick flash ultimate.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:11.860
"You smell like burning!"

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.580
"Get 'em, Tibbers!"

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.160
"Bear hug!"

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:19.040
"Yay, Tibbers!"

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:22.220
All with a skip in her step.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.060
"Hop, skip, jump!"

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:27.800
"What's your favorite aminal? A bear?"

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:32.880
"Beaten by a little girl... ha!"

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:36.740
"I'm rubber and you're... on fire!"

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:41.800
Our runner up, is the maestro of mayhem and madness.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:47.480
"Rules are made to be broken... like buildings! Or people!"

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:53.760
Jinx is known for causing chaos with her multitude of chemtech explosives and advanced weaponry.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:56.960
"Stay still! I'm trying to shoot you!"

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:59.040
"Bullets!"

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:02.940
"What if I had a gun that... shot other guns?"

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:04.960
This blue-haired hellion will blow you up with

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:09.460
her Super Mega Death Rocket, laughing hysterically while she does it.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:13.260
"No need to be scared - or alive."

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:14.660
"Bye bye!"

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:18.160
"See ya!"

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:20.260
"Catch!"

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:24.160
Jinx clearly loves what

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:24.960
she does.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.600
"You know what I call five dead enemies?"

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:30.560
"A great start!"

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:38.040
"I killed Poppy! Who's next?"

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:41.360
And her joy, while twisted, is admirable?

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:46.700
"Guns don't kill people. I mean, until you shoot them. Then they kill everything!"

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:50.580
"I'm wearing lots of belts! For no reason at all."

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:52.040
Okay, she’s a lunatic.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.820
"I'm crazy! Got a doctor's note."

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:57.860
But she at least keeps things interesting for Piltover’s

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:58.440
finest .

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:01.200
"Vi? Stands for stupid."

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:07.360
"Welcome to Snoresville, hat lady! Population: you."

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:11.960
"Now where was I? Oh, right, wreaking havoc!"

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:15.280
Okay guys, we lied in the intro.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:20.900
It turns out that having a single cheeky one-liner will take you to the top of this list.

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:21.940
"Okay."

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:27.320
Because for our first place finish we have none other than the Armordillo RAMMUS!

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:28.440
"Yeah."

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.660
No one really knows what Rammus is.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:32.640
"Hmm."

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:37.660
There are those who speculate that he’s the last of a dying species.

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:38.420
"Right."

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:43.380
The superstitious swear he’s a harbinger of change.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:44.520
"Yeh."

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:50.040
Some even believe that he’s an Ascended being, an ancient god who rolls to Shurima’s

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:52.160
aid in its times of need.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:53.420
"Alright."

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:57.320
We asked him about his thoughts on the rumors.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:58.480
"Hmm."

00:12:59.220 --> 00:12:59.860
"Yeah."

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:01.180
"Alright."

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:06.740
Well one thing’s for sure, Rammus will be rolling his way into your lane and there’s very

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.420
little you can do about it.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:09.000
"Yeah."

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:23.720
(Casting)

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:24.300
"Ok."

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:31.260
Well guys that's our list for this week. Now if you didn't agree with it, I got one line for you.

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:32.580
"Shut your mouth hole!"

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:35.060
"Them badgers are listening."

